# Short-lived branches

Branches are temporary delivery vehicles, not permanent homes for features.

- Open a branch for active work only.
- Once the feature is completed, reviewed, and built/merged (or deliberately abandoned), **close the PR and delete the branch** on remote and locally.
- Do not leave long-lived feature branches sitting open “just in case.”
- Prefer one active feature branch at a time when practical; clean up stale branches before starting the next large effort.
- `main` is the durable line. Everything else should earn its keep by being in progress.
